# BetterRoxas — build-time configuration template
#
# Copy to .env and adjust before running `npm run build` or `npm run package`.
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is git-ignored and is NEVER copied into dist/ or into the release
# archive — these values are consumed while building, not served to browsers.
# There are no server-side secrets in this project: the site is fully static,
# so anything that reaches the browser is public by definition. Do not put
# credentials here expecting them to stay private.

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Canonical site URL
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Used by the React app build (react-app/next.config.js) for absolute URLs.
# No trailing slash. Change this for a staging subdomain deploy.
SITE_URL=https://betterroxas.vercel.app


# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Placeholders — replace before the site goes public
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These are embedded directly in the HTML rather than injected at build time,
# because the site ships as plain static pages with no templating step.
#
# Everything that could be sourced from roxascity.gov.ph, the PSA, the DTI or
# Wikipedia has been filled in (officials, the 47 barangays, the census and
# poverty series, 2024 city finances, CMCI rankings, the city history, the
# official hotline, city hall numbers, email, address and Facebook page).
# What is listed below could NOT be sourced and is still a placeholder.
#
#   Google Analytics measurement ID .... G-XXXXXXXXXX
#     Appears in the <head> of index.html, 403.html, 404.html, 500.html and
#     every page under services/ and service-details/.
#     Find with:  grep -rl "G-XXXXXXXXXX" --include="*.html" .
#     Until it is set to a real Roxas City property, gtag loads but records
#     nothing. Leaving it is safe; setting it to someone else's ID is not.
#
#   PNP / BFP / hospital hotlines ...... NOT PUBLISHED
#     Deliberately absent. Three independent online directories give three
#     different numbers for the Roxas City police station, and two disagree on
#     the fire station; roxascity.gov.ph publishes only the City Emergency
#     Response Team line. Rather than guess, the hotline sections carry 911 and
#     the CERT numbers plus a note. Add the rest only from an official source.
#
#   Department direct lines and emails . NOT PUBLISHED
#     Roxas City publishes a trunkline ((036) 6212-049 / (036) 6516-053) and a
#     single address (roxascitygovph@gmail.com), not per-office contacts, so
#     every department card points at those. Replace with real direct lines
#     when the city publishes them.
#
#   Service fees ....................... STILL SOLANO'S SCHEDULE
#     The peso amounts quoted on the services/ and service-details/ pages were
#     Solano's. Check them against the Roxas City Citizen's Charter:
#     https://roxascity.gov.ph/roxas-city/citizens-charter/
#     Find with:  grep -rn "₱" --include="*.html" services service-details
#
#   Economic indicators ................ NOT PUBLISHED
#     Registered businesses, agricultural land, employment rate, the sector
#     mix and the NTA/local revenue split are not published in a citable form.
#     Those blocks render a "not yet available" notice.
#
#   CMCI per-indicator scores .......... PORTAL-ONLY
#     The 2024 headline rankings are in place. The per-pillar score series is
#     only in the DTI interactive portal, which blocks automated access:
#     https://cmci.dti.gov.ph/lgu-profile.php?lgu=Roxas+(CZ)
#
#   Ordinances / resolutions / projects / news ... EMPTY
#     See https://roxascity.gov.ph/sp-ordinances/ and /sp-resolutions/.
#
#   Quiz site .......... quiz.betterroxas.org
#     PLACEHOLDER — no such deployment exists. Linked from the homepage CTA
#     and every footer. Either stand up the quiz or remove those links.
#     Find with:  grep -rl "quiz.betterroxas.org" .
#
#   Appointment system . roxasmayorsoffice-oasys.com
#     PLACEHOLDER — the Solano site linked a real third-party OASYS booking
#     system. No Roxas City equivalent is known, so this hostname does not
#     resolve. It is the primary CTA in the homepage appointment section.
#     Find with:  grep -rl "roxasmayorsoffice-oasys" .
#
#   Project contact .... volunteer@betterroxas.org, facebook.com/betterroxas
#     PLACEHOLDER — these belong to this civic-tech project, not the city.
#     No mailbox or page exists (the site is on a free vercel.app subdomain,
#     which cannot receive mail).
#
#   Official city Facebook page ........ facebook.com/roxascitycomgroup
#     This one IS real (linked from roxascity.gov.ph/contact). The FB_PAGE_ID
#     repo variable used by .github/workflows/facebook-sync.yml still needs the
#     matching numeric page ID.
#
# The Content-Security-Policy in .htaccess and vercel.json allow-lists the
# third-party origins these depend on. If you point them somewhere new, update
# both or the browser will block them.
